====================================================================================================
 HIGH-MAGNITUDE STRESS: scale a fixed compressed shape up and watch q
====================================================================================================
  base compressed shape S = [7, 9, 13, 16, 18, 36, 48, 66, 72, 126, 156, 280, 312], witness q = 15
  (scale-invariance: L(cS)=L(S), so a dilated far chain has the SAME q -- magnitude does NOT force q up
   UNLESS the shape itself changes. mac-mini's q~log(mag) needs NEW primes at each scale = a LONGER chain,
   but a 13-runner chain has BOUNDED length => bounded #primes => bounded q. THE KEY COUNTING BOUND.)

====================================================================================================
 READING / VERDICT
====================================================================================================
  max witness q over the compressed covering >=7-far families found: 17
  If maxq is BOUNDED (small): compressed >=7-far families ARE census-able at bounded q => the gap-case
  dispatch's >=7-far branch is CLOSED BY THE CENSUS (no tower needed for compressed) -- only the DOMINANT
  (peelable) large runners need the tower/peel. Since 13 runners bound the chain length (hence the #band
  primes, hence q ~ #primes), the compressed witness q is BOUNDED -- the crux dissolves into the census.
DONE.

